<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/slc-skyline.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/slc-skyline-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/slc-skyline.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="shell sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span><a href="/utah-communities/">Communities</a><span class="sep">›</span><span aria-current="page">Salt Lake City</span></nav><p class="kicker">Wasatch Front · Salt Lake County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Salt Lake City, Utah</h1><p class="lede">Utah’s capital mixes century-old brick bungalows, Victorian homes in the Avenues, mid-century ranches on the east bench and downtown high-rises. Each one fails differently in a storm, and each one prices differently in an estimate.</p><div class="row-btns"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/contact-utah-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Salt Lake County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Wasatch Front</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="shell two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="callout"><b>Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Canyon wind</li><li>Hail</li><li>Earthquake (endorsement)</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Burst pipes</li></ul></div>
<h2>Claims we see in Salt Lake City</h2>
<p>Salt Lake City sits at the heart of Salt Lake County, with neighborhoods that climb from the valley floor in Rose Park and Glendale to the foothills of Federal Heights and the East Bench. Summer thunderstorms bring hail and microbursts. Winter brings ice dams on older, poorly insulated roofs and frozen pipes during cold snaps. Canyon winds can hit the northern and eastern neighborhoods hard, as they did in September 2020.</p>
<h2>Storm and seismic history</h2>
<p>On August 11, 1999, a tornado moved through downtown Salt Lake City, the Avenues and Capitol Hill, damaging hundreds of buildings. On March 18, 2020, the magnitude 5.7 Magna earthquake rattled the valley; chimneys and brick parapets were damaged across the west side and in older neighborhoods. Owners who carry earthquake coverage should know their deductible before a claim.</p>
<h2>Housing that shapes the estimate</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sugar House, Liberty Wells and the Avenues:</strong> early 1900s brick bungalows and Victorians with plaster walls, original trim and complex rooflines.</li>
<li><strong>Capitol Hill and Federal Heights:</strong> steep lots, older masonry and expensive access for roof and siding work.</li>
<li><strong>Rose Park and Glendale:</strong> mid-century homes, many with additions and older electrical and plumbing.</li>
<li><strong>Downtown and Central City:</strong> condominiums and mixed-use buildings where HOA master policies and unit-owner policies interact.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What to watch for</h2>
<p>Plaster and lath repairs, historic trim and masonry are routinely underpriced. For condos, check which policy covers interior finishes before assuming the association will handle it.</p>
<h2>Services for Salt Lake City property owners</h2><p>Every Utah Insurance Appraiser service is available in Salt Lake City and across Salt Lake County, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/policy-appraisal-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/canyon-wind-damage-appraisal/">Wind &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/snow-ice-freeze-appraisal/">Snow Load, Ice Dam &amp; Freeze Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/water-pipe-leak-appraisal/">Water &amp; Leak Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul><h2>Questions from Salt Lake City owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you inspect homes in the Avenues and on the East Bench?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Yes. We work throughout Salt Lake City, including hillside neighborhoods where access and steep roofs affect pricing.</p></div></details><details><summary>My condo had a leak from the unit above. Who pays?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>It depends on the HOA’s master policy, the governing documents and your unit-owner policy. We can review the estimates once coverage is sorted out.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby communities</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/utah-communities/west-valley-city/"><small>Nearby</small><span>West Valley City</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" st